  "id": "COMPOUND:29466 - PROTEIN:6311",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Quercetin Dihydrate and Histone deacetylase 5, as it is observed to interact with LoVo cells, which are targeted by multiple variants of Quercetin Dihydrate. These variants, including (3S,4S)-6-[(3S,4S)-4,10-Dihydroxy-7,9-Dimethoxy-3-Methyl-3,4-Dihydro-1H-Benzo[G]Isochromen-5-Yl]-7,9-Dimethoxy-3-Methyl-3,4-Dihydro-1H-Benzo[G]Isochromene-4,10-Diol and N-[(3S,4R,5R,8S,9S,10R,13S,14S,17S)-17-[(1S)-1-(dimethylamino)ethyl]-4-hydroxy-10,13-dimethyl-2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9,11,12,14,15,16,17-tetradecahydro-1H-cyclopenta[a]phenanthren-3-yl]-3,4-dimethylpent-3-enamide, all ultimately target Histone deacetylase 5. This indicates that Quercetin Dihydrate may exert its biological effects through a common mechanism, possibly by inhibiting Histone deacetylase 5 in LoVo cells. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a strong and reliable relationship, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
